Chapter: FailFunResult
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A fail inside a function whose result is a function: the riscv plug typed
 the fail by its function result and built a closure in place of raising,
 so the call of that closure hung (zig-fail-closure, plugs 2.121).

Section: Body

  risky : Integer -> Integer
  risky (n) = if n > 5 then fail "too big" else n

  pick-fn : Integer -> (Integer -> Integer)
  pick-fn (n) = if n > 5 then fail "pick too big" else risky

  plain : Integer -> Integer
  plain (n) = if n > 5 then fail "plain too big" else n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "start"
    trying 1 times
      print-line-uni (show (let f = pick-fn 9 in f 4))
    falling back to
      print-line-uni "fallback"
    on failure
      print-line-uni "failure"
    end
    print-line-uni "end"
  end